summary=json.loads((OUT/'checks_summary.json').read_text()); active=read(OUT/'active_series_by_year.csv'); mat=read(OUT/'selection_recomputed.csv')
parts=['# INPACT Policy Timeline — independent content audit',f'\nAudit date: **31 October 2026 (Europe/Dublin)**. Historical analysis window: 2000–2023. The prompt filename says 2028; it is a filename, not the audit date.\n',
'## 1. Audit conclusion and boundaries\n',
'The release is computationally consistent in the checks performed, but it should not yet be presented as a fully verified legal chronology. Five date/identity conflicts could change timeline values; several generic labels overstate what the data establish. All corrections below are **proposals only**. No release, app, database, score, original extract, branch or commit was changed. Only audit outputs were written.\n',
'Evidence distinguishes accessed official text from search-index excerpts and failed access. VERIFIED below means the expressly stated claims/basis were corroborated; it does **not** certify every historical amendment, exemption, legal commencement or source narrative. UNVERIFIED is an evidence limitation, not proof of error. Indexed-only evidence and unresolved source-phase boundaries must be reviewed before data corrections. Residual bundles have computational, not legal, verification.\n',
'Local content was inspected in templates, editorial/glossary text, API payloads, read-only SQLite, and HTTP responses generated by Django’s test client. All 8 scoped pages and 47 profile URLs returned HTTP 200. This is **not a browser rendering or interaction test**. No database reload, migrations, Django test suite or deployment occurred, as those belong to the approval phase.\n',
'### Recomputed totals against the local app\n',table(['Measure','Recomputed','Local app','Result'],[[k,v,summary['app_stats'].get(k,'not a displayed total'), 'MATCH' if summary['app_stats'].get(k)==v else 'Definition note'] for k,v in summary['recomputed'].items()]),
'There are **39 distinct IDs including 5 analytical bundles**, and **34 core families**. The latter expand to **42 core policy–sector series**; five residual series bring the panel to **47 × 24 = 1,128 annual rows**. EEA raw type field independently confirms 98 Single and 6 Group records. The catalogue also holds 17 unique non-core member families; it must not be counted as the displayed core.\n',
'### Multi-sector mapping\n',table(['Policy ID','Affected sectors'],[[p,', '.join(s)] for p,s in sorted(summary['multi_sector'].items())]),
'Four two-sector families add four series, and carbon tax/ETS each add two: 34 + 4 + 4 = 42. Carbon-tax starts differ legitimately (2009 transport; 2010 buildings/industry), as do ETS starts (2005 stationary; 2012 aviation). Names are consistent across these slices. Residual-member sectors are detailed separately in residual_member_verification.csv.\n',
'### Finding counts\n',table(['Severity','Distinct findings'],sorted(Counter(f['severity'] for f in F).items())),table(['Verdict','Distinct findings'],sorted(Counter(f['verdict'] for f in F).items())),
'These counts cover F01–F21, not every repeated profile or annual row. Separately, family-level verdict counts (34 core + 17 residual-member families + 5 bundles, one verdict per identity) are:\n',table(['Verdict','Identities'],sorted(Counter(v['verdict'] for v in J.values()).items())),
'### Live reference comparison\n',
'The accessible live overview at https://inpact-epa.vercel.app/policy/ shows the same headline counts (34, 47, 5, 115, 64, 104/98/6, 7→43), retrospective caveat, emissions figures and growth wording as local content. No difference was observed in those items. The web response was an indexed snapshot labelled crawled three weeks ago; this is not proof of current deployment parity. Direct live API comparison was attempted but the local environment failed DNS resolution. Other live pages/profiles were not certified equal.\n',
'## 2. Policy-by-policy verification\n',
'The complete 47-row **policy_register.csv** contains every requested field: original start/end and basis, all annual implementation sources and assumed years, mechanism, instrument, multi-sector flag, layer, OECD match, aggregation role, fixed members, original citations, milestones/lineage and profile route. **policy_verification.csv** adds verdict, severity, evidence URL/section/access date and proposed correction to those same fields. The following table is a compact human-readable view; start/end values are selected dataset dates, not automatically legal dates.\n',
table(['ID / policy','Sector; layer; mechanism','Start–end / basis','OECD match / aggregation','Verdict; severity','Assessment; correction; evidence'],[[r['policy_id']+' — '+r['policy_name'],r['sector']+'; '+r['layer']+'; '+r['mechanism'],r['start_year']+'–'+(r['end_year'] or 'open')+'; '+r['start_year_basis'],r['capmf_code']+' / '+r['match_confidence']+'; '+r['aggregation_role'],r['verdict']+'; '+r['severity'],r['assessment_and_proposed_correction']+' '+r['evidence']] for r in verification]),
'### Policies represented only inside residuals\n',
'One row per member identity below; every member-sector combination, its dates, original source citation and scores is retained in residual_member_verification.csv. Passing bundle arithmetic does not validate a member’s legal dates.\n',
table(['ID / policy','Sectors','Selected period','Verdict; severity','Assessment / evidence'],[[pid+' — '+next(r['policy_name'] for r in memberverify if r['policy_id']==pid),', '.join(r['sector'] for r in memberverify if r['policy_id']==pid),next(r['start_year']+'–'+(r['end_year'] or 'open') for r in memberverify if r['policy_id']==pid),J[pid]['verdict']+'; '+J[pid]['severity'],J[pid]['assessment_and_proposed_correction']+' '+J[pid]['evidence']] for pid in sorted(memberids)]),
'## 3. Timeline and selection reproducibility\n',
'### Checks actually executed\n',table(['Check','Row comparisons'],sorted(summary['checks'].items())),
f"\nNo discrepancies in those comparisons: {summary['discrepancies_by_field']}. The empty timeline_discrepancies.csv is the machine-check result, not an assertion that factual dates are correct. Database/source comparisons found {summary['database_differences']} differences in checked names, dates, codes, membership and annual status/source/score fields. Post-expiry implementation is independently checked against the end-year level and half-life. All protected-file hashes matched before/after execution.\n",
'### Factual date discrepancies (proposed; not applied)\n',
'factual_date_discrepancies.csv lists every affected policy–sector–year, field, proposed expected value, actual value and CSV record locator for F01–F05. These are distinct from formula consistency. Representative records are shown below; a changed member date can also change the containing residual mean. Proposed dates depend on confirming family identity and phase; no counterfactual score is presented as an approved value.\n',
table(['Finding','Policy / sector','Year','Field','Expected / proposed','Actual','CSV record'],[[r['finding'],r['policy_id']+' / '+r['sector'],r['year'],r['field'],r['expected_proposed'],r['actual'],r['location']] for r in dateissues if r['year']=='2000']),
'### Annual active-series counts\n',table(['Year','Active series'],[[r['year'],r['active_series']] for r in active]),
'The overview growth claim is supported by this release: counts remain seven through 2004; all net expansion begins later. It is a count of selected series, not a complete history of Irish policy adoption. The 2022→2023 fall from 44 to 43 reflects the recorded boiler-phase expiry, not evidence that boiler standards were repealed. Chart code filters the same active status arrays.\n',
'### Assumptions, changes and boundaries\n',
'assumed_years.csv lists **every assumed annual core/bundle row**, including structural zeros. policy_register.csv lists assumed years by series. Parameters agree with all 12 config classes. Methods uses the same mid-year linear ramp; framework legal-presence fallback is explicitly distinct. Post-expiry decay matches the stored end-year implementation, not a backcast OECD value. The timeline hatch condition excludes pre-start zeros and residual means (F15).\n',
'implementation_changes.csv lists source switches after activation and changes of at least 0.20 on the implementation scale. This threshold is an audit screen, not a change to release rules. Values tie to the same-year raw source or deterministic assumed profile; causal/legal explanations for individual OECD jumps were not inferred. All 418 OECD-derived rows across main and member panels match usable same-year scores/10, using the distinct-code mean and excluding K/M. No carry-forward/backcast found. Pre-start rows are structural zeros.\n',
'Original pre-2000 proxy years (1991 Part L dwellings, 1995 labels, 1996 appliance standards, 1999 car labels) are retained; LIEN is the exception requiring historical reconciliation. No annual values outside 2000–2023 occur. Planned EEA variants are retained as provenance, not separate active core IDs. This verifies panel construction, not the truth of every source historical/planned classification. Fixed residual memberships contain no simultaneous core member-series duplicates.\n',
'### Eligibility, materiality and source priority\n',
'All five recorded Boolean tests recompute eligible exactly: A mitigation, B Ireland, C identifiable instrument/framework, D identified start, E active in the window. Of 115 source candidates, 68 are deduplicated EEA identities and 47 are positive OECD level-3 categories. 44 EEA + 20 OECD candidates pass. There are 27 EEA core and 17 EEA residual candidates, plus 20 eligible OECD candidates; their overlapping identities reconcile to 34 core families. These are source-candidate counts, not additive policy-family counts.\n',
table(['Sector','Eligible / positive / selected','Reported ranking total kt','Selected kt','Share','Recomputed membership/totals'],[[r['sector'],r['eligible']+' / '+r['positive']+' / '+r['selected'],r['ranking_total'],r['selected_total'],r['share'] or 'not assessable',r['membership_matches']+'/'+r['totals_match']] for r in mat]),
'The 90% rule is reproduced from eligible source candidates, descending positive estimates, including the measure crossing the threshold. The reported totals may overlap and are never summed into a national effect. source_estimate_priority.csv checks all 44 eligible EEA candidates against the selected raw workbook record: first numeric ex-post estimate, then 2025, then 2030, preserving zero/negative values. Ineligible/planned records are excluded from this priority test because they never enter ranking. The selection tests themselves are judgement/source classifications; Boolean consistency does not independently re-prove eligibility.\n',
'Overview, Methods decision text, About and the retrospective_selection flag all contain the selection-bias caveat. About says recent assessments but omits the explicit 2024–2030 range; adding it would improve precision, not repair a missing caveat. OECD score categories/labels and flags match the supplied raw export: 56 level-3, 130 level-4, 1990–2023; A normal, E estimated, K included elsewhere, M missing because data cannot exist. Dictionary “not applicable” is a looser paraphrase of M; use the source definition consistently.\n',
'## 4. Context and wording findings\n',table(['ID; severity; verdict','Page; source location','Current text/value','Problem','Proposed correction','Evidence'],[[f['id']+'; '+f['severity']+'; '+f['verdict'],f['page']+'; '+f['location'],f['current_text'],f['problem'],f['suggested_text_or_action'],f['evidence']] for f in F]),
'### Context that is supported, not a defect\n',
'EPA Table 4 supports all supplied 2023 sector numbers and their building/industry aggregations. The sum of rounded sector entries differs from the reported total by 0.001 Mt; that is rounding, not an error. “Electricity” uses Energy Industries (including refining), which is disclosed. Agriculture has exactly two individual families (LESS and liming) and one bundle (crude-protein reduction). The supplied OECD export has no direct agriculture/waste/LULUCF stringency category. This describes the export’s scope, not absence of policy in those sectors.\n',
'The 41.0% renewable-generation statistic is supported by EPA and is not the import-inclusive share of supply. Frameworks, portfolios and residuals are non-additive; ordinal coverage/bindingness, repeated selection savings, CAPMF design proxies and assumed ramps are stated conventions, not numerical defects. Financial support labelled L3 is a modelling taxonomy decision; ACA could be classified as L2 in another taxonomy, but that alone does not establish an error. “Liming” is a mitigation pathway rather than a uniquely named programme; author clarification is needed.\n',
'### Dates and milestone completeness\n',
'Do not replace a disclosed proxy year merely because a legal adoption/application date differs. For 2021 legislation, add commencement; for council distinguish enactment and establishment; for carbon budgets distinguish accounting period and effective programme. The first programme’s provisional third budget must remain labelled provisional. For MAC, earlier leakage rules do not invalidate the selected 2011 high-GWP phase. For car standards, 2009 adoption and 2012 compliance differ legitimately.\n',
'AER/REFIT/RESS need a fuller component chronology before the portfolio can be called legally verified. REFIT1 announcement (2006), approval (2007), REFIT2/3 opening (2012), application closure and PSO support end are different dates. The accessed current gov.ie page lists support end dates 31 December 2027, 2032 and 2030; an indexed older consolidated provision gives 2030 for REFIT2. This conflict must be resolved against the applicable amendment and historical cutoff, not silently chosen. These future support end dates are contextual and must not activate post-2023 observations.\n',
'BER does not appear as a separate selected family. Treat a possible addition as scope/selection review, not a missing-row error. Likewise, possible broader agricultural, forestry, waste, transport-infrastructure or adaptation coverage should be discussed as selection limitations; do not add policies or change eligibility in this audit.\n',
'### Bibliography and source quality\n',
'Nachtigall 2022 and Kruse 2022 metadata match OECD; Rosenow/Bayer 2017 metadata match publisher. EPA 2026 inventory matches Table 4. Martin et al. needs its complete title (F20). Stechemesser metadata was cross-checked in PubMed, but publisher-level full-text verification was not completed; treat this as corroboration, not certification. Remaining theoretical references (Baumol/Oates, Goulder/Parry, Jaffe/Stavins, Allcott/Greenstone, Couture/Gagnon, Fankhauser et al., OECD/JRC and IPCC) were not fully independently checked at passage level and remain UNVERIFIED for exact claim support. Citation existence does not validate researcher-assigned timing or score assumptions.\n',
'The source-reference table dates the LIEN webpage to 2019, whereas the opened page is dated 21 November 2018; correct that metadata during an approved citation pass. Source citations often point to a registry homepage or a broad document, rather than the specific instrument/section. Add precise locators and preserve evidence-access limitations instead of presenting every reference as fully verified. The UI cleaner replaces AI-generated timing provenance with “specified by the study”; authors should confirm they have actually adopted and validated those assumptions before using that attribution. No parameter change is proposed.\n',
'## 5. Items needing author input\n',
'1. Approve or reject F01–F05 individually after choosing whether each row represents programme inception, application window, funding completion, service activation or a modelled-effects phase. Data/score changes need a documented scope decision; none have been applied.\n2. Resolve CHP 2010/2011 closure, Public Sector Programme 2009/2010/2011, National Home Energy Upgrade 2021/2022 and boiler/SME 2022 expiry. Preserve EEA source quotations.\n3. Supply/identify historical primary records for remaining UNVERIFIED families, exact petroleum saving provisions, full Part L/appliance vintage crosswalk, original AER/2005 portfolio basis, biofuel excise predecessors and rate changes. Official statute/gov.ie direct opens returned 403 in several cases; indexed text was used only for the claims it exposes.\n4. Confirm whether the selected climate-act start basis is enactment or commencement; the annual 2021 value is unchanged either way. Obtain the original carbon-budget programme document to finish checking provisional-budget detail.\n5. Resolve REFIT2 future support-period conflict against the relevant PSO amendment and freeze contextual statements to the historical cutoff.\n6. Confirm researcher ownership of the timing assumptions and intended meaning of liming as a programme/pathway.\n7. Complete remaining bibliography passage checks and browser interaction review before publication.\n',
'## 6. Reproduction and deliverables\n',
'Run from the repository with the supplied Python interpreter:\n\n```powershell\n& C:/ProgramData/anaconda3/python.exe -B audit/scripts/check_policy_data.py\n& C:/ProgramData/anaconda3/python.exe -B audit/scripts/write_audit_report.py\n```\n\nThe first script uses SQLite URI mode=ro and does not call the data loader. It writes input SHA-256 hashes, checks_summary.json, policy_register.csv, annual/assumed/source-priority/decay/selection/jump comparisons and page checks. The second assembles this report, evidence_register.csv, findings.csv, policy_verification.csv and residual_member_verification.csv from the fixed human-readable assessments above. Evidence retrieval is not replayed by the scripts. Counts and row locators should be regenerated if the release changes.\n',
'CSV record numbers include header row 1; multiline quoted cells mean record numbers are not always physical text-line numbers. Text findings use physical file:line locators. The policy register is the full field-level table; the report is the review narrative. No DOCX correction report is produced before approval because no corrections have been made.\n',
'## Evidence register\n',table(['ID','URL','Section / locator','Access','Evidence summary'],[[s['source_id'],s['url'],s['section'],s['access']+'; '+s['access_date'],s['evidence_summary']] for s in S.values()]),
'\n**Stop point:** audit only. Await approval of specific findings before changing app text/data, rebuilding SQLite or committing corrections.\n']
